          "Camel caravans, each comprising several thousand animals, traversed the desert in convoys, transporting bars of salt south from the desert pans and bringing back gold, ivory, and slaves from the rainforest kingdoms of Mali.",
          "Scholars from across the Islamic world accompanied the trade and accumulated in the city's three principal mosques, where they compiled commentaries on law, astronomy, medicine, and theology that circulated throughout the Islamic universe.",
          "At its peak Timbuktu accommodated nearly a hundred thousand inhabitants and amassed a library reputed to contain several hundred thousand handwritten manuscripts.",
          "When the first European traveller finally reached Timbuktu in the early nineteenth century he found the wells silted and the libraries dispersed, but the manuscripts had not vanished.",
