          "In the same century, a librarian named Eratosthenes calculated the circumference of the planet using nothing but a vertical stick, the length of its shadow at noon in two different cities, and elementary geometry.",
          "His result deviated from the modern satellite measurement by less than two per cent.",
          "The ancient Greeks had demonstrated that the human mind, applied with sufficient discipline, could establish both the principles of self-government and the dimensions of the planet itself, using almost no equipment at all."
