        "number": "10.1",
        "title": "The Bering Land Bridge",
        "blocks": [
          "Across multiple ice ages the level of the world's oceans dropped sufficiently that a wide land corridor emerged between Siberia and Alaska, exposing dry tundra where the Bering Sea now reaches.",
          "Bands of Asian hunters tracking herds of mammoth and bison crossed eastward over the exposed bridge and within a few thousand years their descendants had populated every habitable region of the Americas from the Yukon to Tierra del Fuego.",
          "The same hunters appear to have annihilated, in combination with the warming climate, virtually every ice-age megafauna species they encountered.",
          "The mammoth, the giant ground sloth, the sabre-toothed cat, the giant short-faced bear, the American camel, and dozens of additional large mammals vanished from the fossil record within a few thousand years of human arrival.",
          "The continent that received the first Americans had already been reshaped by them before they themselves were established within it."
        ],
