          "The Maya constructed stepped stone pyramids that ascended above the surrounding canopy, devised a writing system of glyphs that recorded astronomy and royal genealogies, and articulated a calendar so precise that the accumulated error after a millennium amounted to less than a single day.",
          "Their astronomers had calculated the orbit of Venus with sufficient accuracy to predict its appearances centuries in advance.",
          "Then, across roughly a single century, almost every major Maya city in the southern lowlands was simply abandoned.",
          "The population dispersed into smaller communities and the surrounding jungle reclaimed the platforms.",
          "Archaeologists continue to debate whether drought, internal warfare, ecological collapse, or some combination of these terminated the lowland Maya, but no single explanation has accounted for the full scale of the abandonment."
